 "narrative": [
  "The business economics major is a collaborative, interdisciplinary degree program between the Rady School of Management and the Department of Economics.",
  "While we require business economics majors to take MATH 10A-B-C, we recommend that business economics students take MATH 20A-B-C.",
  "To receive a bachelor of science degree in business economics, no more than one upper-division economics course and one upper-division Rady School of Management course may be taken externally from UC San Diego and be counted toward the major.",
  "To graduate with a major, a minimum GPA of 2.0 is required in upper-division courses used to satisfy major requirements.",
  "All courses must be taken for a letter grade and passed with a grade of C– (C minus), or better, with the exception of ECON 195P, ECON 198, and ECON 199, for which P/NP grading is mandatory.",
  "No more than twelve units of ECON 195P, ECON 198, and ECON 199 taken P/NP may be counted toward major requirements. ECON 195P may only be taken twice for credit (eight units).",
  "Also described on the Rady School of Management page (https://catalog.ucsd.edu/curric/MGT-ug.html, \"The Business Economics Major (BSc)\"), which lists the finance core course as \"MGT 180/180R\" rather than MGT 180 and omits the ECON P/NP exceptions from its grade rules."
 ]
